+### [Hero-like Octree Traversal](5492-hero-like-octree-traversal.md)
+Hero-like Octree Traversal is a depth-first search (DFS) algorithm for ray-tracing octrees that determines the order in which child voxels are penetrated by a ray using a 2x2x2 voxel test. It generates child addresses via arithmetic and logical operations, allowing the traversal to skip hidden objects by yielding the first terminal voxel hit. It differs from its siblings by explicitly computing the traversal order of children at each node using bitmask logic (VMASK, CHILDMASK) and maintaining state on a stack to resume traversal, rather than relying on neighbor-finding or bottom-up approaches. [Hero-like Octree Traversal](5492-hero-like-octree-traversal.md)
